<spell-notebook "placeholder theming">
	<header level="1">
		Placeholder
		<header>A placeholder is used to reserve space for content that soon will appear in a layout.</>
	</>
	<placeholder-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-placeholder-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or
			on the inner box through `::part(placeholder)`; every shape inside follows. They inherit into the shadow roots,
			where the sheet reads each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- A single shape takes them too, on its own element or `::part()`.
			- The colours are tints of the ink colour, so they suit any surface in either scheme.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every placeholder on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-placeholder-duration: 3s;
			}
			/* one region */
			.sidebar {
			  --ui-placeholder-max-width: 40em;
			  --ui-placeholder-radius: 0;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`fluid` lifts the `--ui-placeholder-max-width` cap whatever you set. Never set the `--_ui-placeholder-*` names:
				they're the sheet's private plumbing.
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-placeholder" playground>
				<ui-placeholder>
					<ui-placeholder-header image>
						<ui-placeholder-line></>
						<ui-placeholder-line></>
					</>
					<ui-placeholder-paragraph>
						<ui-placeholder-line length="medium"></>
						<ui-placeholder-line length="short"></>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Each theme of the set (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes a placeholder's colours through the
			shared tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
